  "an2.138:1.3": "In the Pali these two phrases do not grammatically parallel, suggesting that they are quotes. “Cleansing your own mind” (_sacittavodāna_) doesn’t occur elsewhere exactly, but the very similar _sacittapariyodapana_ is found in the famous verses known as Ovāda Pātimokkha ([dn14:3.28.8](), [dhp183:3]()). “Not grasping at anything in the world” concludes each section of the Satipaṭṭhāna Sutta ([mn10:5.3]()). ",
